  "notes": [
    "Estimator scope: wages, self-employment, interest, dividends, capital gains, retirement, Social Security, unemployment, net rental and other income; standard or itemized deduction (SALT cap, medical 7.5% floor and charitable 0.5% floor applied; the larger of the two is used); the non-itemizer charitable deduction (charity entries are treated as cash gifts to qualifying charities); child tax credit; SE tax, additional Medicare tax and NIIT.",
    "Not modelled: AMT, QBI deduction, EITC, education and other credits, the 2025–2028 senior/tips/overtime/car-loan deductions, passive-loss limits, credit for other dependents, the 2026 overall limitation on itemized deductions for the top bracket, the 60%/30% AGI limits on charitable gifts. Enter other credits as user amounts.",
    "Roth IRA contributions are not deductible and are not an itemized or adjustment kind; traditional IRA contributions are adjustments (ira).",
    "Tax is computed with the Rev. Proc. 2025-32 rate schedules (the Tax Computation Worksheet method); the IRS tax tables for income under $100,000 use $50 bands and can differ by a few dollars.",
    "ordinary_dividends means non-qualified ordinary dividends (box 1a minus box 1b).",
    "All results are estimates."
  ],
